# Production build settings — PLAN §5.3.
#
# The published app is static hosting: it cannot open a TCP socket to APRS-IS, so Mode C fell back
# to the recording on every deploy. This points it at the hosted relay instead — a container that
# holds the APRS connection and fans it out over Server-Sent Events, which is the one piece of this
# project that genuinely needs a long-lived process.
#
# ⚠️ Production only, on purpose. In dev the value stays unset so the app uses `/ogn/stream` through
# the Vite proxy and a relay running on the developer's own machine — otherwise every local run
# would silently depend on the cloud, and a local change to the relay could not be tested at all.
#
# No secret here: the URL is public, the stream is public, and the data is anonymised at the relay
# before it is sent (PLAN §2.2.3). The relay restricts CORS to the published origin, so host your
# own — `Dockerfile` builds exactly this relay and it runs happily on a single small container.
#
# Left unset on purpose in the template: without it the published app reports live traffic as
# unavailable and shows the recorded flight instead, badged as a recording. That is a correct and
# honest state, not a failure.
# VITE_OGN_RELAY_URL=https://<your-relay-host>/ogn/stream
